---
// The Vilij — a photo tile sitting in the areas grid alongside the area cards.
//
// `framed` is the rounded, shadowed treatment used on the content pages.
// The homepage uses the unframed variant for its village illustration.
//
// Damien, 30 Jul 2026: "Louie on the beach image needs to be the same size as
// all the rest of the blocks and so does the one of Steph and grandson", and on
// /hall, "need to be full size blocks to complete the grid look."
//
// They were not, because the framed wrapper carried `align-self:start` and the
// image `height:auto` — so the tile sized itself to the photo's own aspect ratio
// and left a gap underneath wherever the cards in its row were taller. The tile
// now stretches to the row like every other grid item, and the photo covers it.
//
// The image is absolutely positioned on purpose. Left in flow it would
// contribute its own height back to the wrapper, which is the circular
// constraint that made `height:100%` unreliable here; out of flow, the
// wrapper's height comes from the grid row alone. `min-height` is the floor for
// the single-column case at <=600px, where the row has no taller sibling to
// stretch to and would otherwise collapse.
//
// Note this crops. The photos are landscape and the blocks are not, so cover
// takes the middle of the frame: p_beach (840x500) and p_grand (760x480) hold up
// fine, but p_jose (494x335) is both the smallest and the widest and loses the
// most. A taller crop of that one would be worth having.
//
// SEO-REVIEW §2 — the framed variant pins both width and height in CSS, so the
// attributes below cannot move it; they only reserve the box early. The unframed
// variant is `width:100%;height:auto`, where the attributes supply the aspect
// ratio the browser would otherwise have to download the file to learn. Both
// tiles sit well below the fold, so both lazy-load.
import { imageSize } from "../data/imageSizes";

interface Props {
  label: string;
  img: string;
  alt: string;
  framed?: boolean;
}
const { label, img, alt, framed = true } = Astro.props;
const size = imageSize(img);
const wrapper = framed
  ? "position:relative;border-radius:18px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 10px 28px rgba(40,80,90,0.12);align-self:stretch;min-height:260px;"
  : "display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:10px;";
---
<Fragment set:html={` <!-- ${label} --> `} />
<div style={wrapper}>
  <img src={img} alt={alt} width={size?.w} height={size?.h} loading="lazy" decoding="async" style={framed
    ? "position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;"
    : "width:100%;height:auto;display:block;"} />
</div>
